index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..afdda2a67efb92d505481ab9030d048025314ea1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,147 @@
+# Seminormalized Hadamard-vector completion
+
+| profile | value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | **B — no-tool compression** |
+| Native domain | combinatorics |
+| Object regime | finite discrete |
+| Computational core | exact linear algebra |
+| Certificate | integer tuple: a balanced `+/-1` vector |
+| Intended intuition | change of variables: signed Walsh characters on binary row tags |
+| Domain essentiality | native; no reduction |
+
+This generator turns [Suksmono, *Probabilistic Construction and Analysis of
+Seminormalized Hadamard Matrices*](https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.09368) into an
+exact completion task.  The solver receives an unordered partial system of
+pairwise-orthogonal sign columns, including the all-ones column, and must add
+one balanced sign vector orthogonal to every displayed column.  `verify()`
+checks the alphabet, balance, and integer inner products directly; it neither
+reads the planted answer nor invokes a theorem or numerical solver.
+
+## Why the instances are known and why this is Track B
+
+Equation (3) and Lemma 1 give Sylvester's Kronecker construction at every
+power-of-two order.  Generation builds that matrix first, deletes `d`
+nonconstant columns, independently negates and reorders the others, randomly
+renames output coordinates, and carries one deleted column as the certificate.
+This is a transformation of a known instance, never a search for a completion.
+Definitions 9 and 11 and Section 3's Algorithms 1–2 supply the exact native
+vector-selection problem.
+
+An efficient method exists, so this is explicitly not Track A.  The reference
+implementation forms the public orthogonality equations, performs exact
+Gauss–Jordan elimination modulo 1,000,003, and enumerates the `2^d` assignments
+to its free coordinates.  Its complexity is `O(n^3 + 2^d n d)`; at the current
+shipping preset `n=128,d=12` it solved 8/8 instances with a measured mean of
+8,171,786 modular operations and 2.010 seconds (maximum 9,479,439 operations).
+That is routine for a computer and not a hand calculation.  Once the Sylvester
+change of variables is noticed, unit auxiliary tags identify each Walsh
+frequency and a missing character can be written with at most 127 exact sign
+negations.  Section 3 also documents the paper's own probabilistic route:
+Table 1 reports 84,081 average trials for selecting only the twelfth column at
+order 24.
+
+## Worked demo (`seed=1`)
+
+The smallest instance is genuinely hand-solvable:
+
+```text
+SEMINORMALIZED HADAMARD-VECTOR COMPLETION
+n=4; three mutually orthogonal displayed columns, one the unity column.
+Each row is output_label : auxiliary_tag | displayed signs.
+
+00 : 11 | +++
+01 : 10 | +--
+10 : 01 | ++-
+11 : 00 | +-+
+```
+
+The answer is `[-1, -1, 1, 1]` in output-label order.
+
+```python
+verify(inst, [-1, -1, 1, 1])
+# (True, "ok")
+verify(inst, [1, -1, 1, 1])
+# (False, "candidate is not balanced: it must contain n/2 of each sign")
+```
+
+## Difficulty and gates
+
+| preset | `n` | deleted `d` | visible columns | status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 4 | 1 | 3 | hand example; hardening skips it |
+| easy | 32 | 8 | 24 | first oracle rung |
+| medium | 64 | 10 | 54 | escalation rung |
+| hard | 128 | 12 | 116 | current `SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY` |
+
+An earlier construction using natural output-coordinate order was rejected by
+G6 because residual greedy solved 8/8.  Randomly renaming output coordinates,
+while retaining public auxiliary tags, reduces that same attack to 0/8 without
+hiding the intended invariant.
+
+| gate | measured result |
+|---|---|
+| G1 | 20/20 planted answers verified across all presets |
+| G2 | 5/5 corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
+| G3 | tagged fenced JSON round-trips exactly |
+| G4 | 0/200,000 valid structure-aware balanced guesses |
+| G5 | shipping sampled density 0; 4,096-restart baseline failed; demo has exactly 2/6 answers |
+| G6 | six attacks, each 0/8; reference elimination 8/8 |
+| G7 | order 256 builds and its carried answer verifies |
+| G8 | 120/120 symmetry/key checks and 120/120 carried-witness checks; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9(c) | 321 characters, 161 estimated tokens, 128 atoms, 127 intended exact operations |
+
+## Oracle loop and G9 diagnostics
+
+The required script was invoked, but OpenRouter rejected every request before a
+model ran with HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)`.  These are API
+errors, not model failures, and therefore are not claimed as hardening evidence.
+
+| run | preset | scorable solved/attempts | result |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| bare | easy | 0/0 | infrastructure error; four calls rejected |
+| structural hint | hard-only copy | 0/0 | pending retry |
+| placebo hint | hard-only copy | 0/0 | pending retry |
+
+Consequently `hinted - placebo` is not yet measurable.  The structural hint is
+only “the displayed signed columns are Walsh characters on the binary auxiliary
+tags”; it names the invariant and gives no procedure.  The measured size and
+effort caps above pass independently of this diagnostic.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+import importlib.util
+
+path = "results/1606.09368/gen_1606_09368.py"
+spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("hadamard_gen", path)
+g = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
+spec.loader.exec_module(g)
+
+params = g.DIFFICULTY[g.SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY]
+inst = g.make_instance(seed=7, **params)
+question = g.render(inst)
+answer = g.parse_answer("<answer>" + __import__("json").dumps(inst["answer"]) + "</answer>")
+assert g.verify(inst, answer) == (True, "ok")
+```
+
+From the repository root, emit instances with:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/emit.sh 1606.09368 20 hard
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+The public tags deliberately make this a compression benchmark; a solver that
+recognizes Walsh characters can solve it efficiently.  The 0/200,000 estimate
+is only for the declared uniform prior over already-balanced vectors.  It does
+not prove an exact shipping solution count or average-case hardness.  The
+canonical key uses exact pair-correlation and weighted-triangle histograms; it
+is invariant under the tested row/column relabellings and sign operations but,
+like any incomplete graph invariant, could collide on nonisomorphic systems.
+The panel did not run a general SAT/SMT encoding because exact elimination is a
+strictly more direct successful reference method for these linear constraints.
+Most importantly, the external four-vendor oracle and both G9 prompt arms must
+be rerun when the supplied OpenRouter key has quota; until then this directory
+is locally verified but not eligible to claim a script-owned `hardened` verdict.
