\section{Probabilistic Analysis}

In this section, we will derive the orthogonal probability $p_{\perp}$, which is the probability that two randomly SH vectors $\vec{v}_1,\vec{v}_2 \in V$ are orthogonal. We also calculate the lower- and upper- bound estimates of $p_{\perp}$, based on permutation and combination approximation. Then, we address the distribution of H-matrices across order based on known number of unique H-matrices and compare with the results of probabilistic analysis based on $p_{\perp}$.
