/tmp/tmp.PvTzB0f0ut/src/RND_Sect1_Introduction.tex:15:In this paper, when the order of a matrix or a vector is clear from the context of discussion, which in most of cases are $4k$ for a positive integer $k$, it will not be written. Furthermore, we say a square matrix $\vec{A}$ of size $m \times m$ as an $m$-order matrix $\vec{A}$, and an $m$-length or of size $m \times 1$ vector $\vec{v}$ as an $m$-order vector $\vec{v}$. However, when the order needs to be explicitly displayed, it is written as a left-superscript. Therefore, an $m$-order matrix $\vec{H}$ will be written as ${}^m\vec{H}$, and similarly, an $m$-order vector $\vec{v}$ will be written as ${}^m\vec{v}$. 
